---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="The Little AI Company is an independent software studio. We build pro-human AI tools: the person stays in control and keeps learning."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="display-l">About</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Little AI Company is an independent software studio run by Jeff Kazzee. We
        build small tools for people who use AI and intend to stay in charge of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 class="heading">The position</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Most AI products are built to take work off your hands. Some of that is
          useful. Past a point it takes your judgment with it, and you end up trusting
          output you can't inspect from a system you can't stop.
        </p>
        <p>
          We build the other kind. A tool of ours shows you where a claim came from,
          keeps its state in files you can open, and waits for your approval before it
          changes anything that matters. It should leave you sharper than it found you.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's the whole company. Everything we ship is open source and runs on your
          machine.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 class="heading">What we don't do</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="lanes">
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>No hosted memory</dt>
          <dd>We don't keep your data on our servers. We don't have servers.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>No telemetry</dt>
          <dd>Our tools don't phone home, and neither does this site.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>No autopilot</dt>
          <dd>Nothing ships that acts on your behalf without a gate you can see.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="lane">
          <dt>No courses</dt>
          <dd>
            Jeff's guides and workshops on second brains and Zo Computer live on his own
            account at <a href="https://github.com/Jeff-Kazzee">github.com/Jeff-Kazzee</a>.
            This company is the software.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
</style>
